vative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({sin}^{2}⁡x)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{|{sin}^{2}⁡x|\\sqrt{1+{({sin}^{2}⁡x)}^{2}}}]\\cdot {({sin}^{2}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{sin}^{2}⁡x\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{4}⁡x}}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{4}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{4}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-404a0d84-133e-5c7d-befe-504815e54709"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-404a0d84-133e-5c7d-befe-504815e54709" :answer-field/id #uuid "404a0d84-133e-5c7d-befe-504815e54709" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ede78e57-6cef-5911-b9d8-27b6208cdab6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ede78e57-6cef-5911-b9d8-27b6208cdab6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ede78e57-6cef-5911-b9d8-27b6208cdab6" :answer/id #uuid "ede78e57-6cef-5911-b9d8-27b6208cdab6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\cot x}{\\sqrt{1+\\sin^4 x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-da5d7294-c739-5f77-ae4a-e6ad7eaa5e42" :question/id #uuid "da5d7294-c739-5f77-ae4a-e6ad7eaa5e42" :question/math-academy-id "q-95513" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\sqrt{x},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{|\\sqrt{x}|\\sqrt{1+{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{x})^{′} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2x\\sqrt{1+x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35e861d8-35db-5fbf-9625-ffbf188c6d98"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35e861d8-35db-5fbf-9625-ffbf188c6d98" :answer-field/id #uuid "35e861d8-35db-5fbf-9625-ffbf188c6d98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-beffe3d3-af5d-5d96-88c7-8a69f5ac0e3c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-beffe3d3-af5d-5d96-88c7-8a69f5ac0e3c" "answer-2c01ef25-72cb-56e3-850f-f5b42b06cd2d" "answer-5fffb130-9b68-531c-b156-aeb0418f3acf" "answer-578cf9cd-0a48-54e7-91c9-36e1da945aea" "answer-e95dd13d-e8b2-5d40-a5e7-9171f4068764"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-beffe3d3-af5d-5d96-88c7-8a69f5ac0e3c" :answer/id #uuid "beffe3d3-af5d-5d96-88c7-8a69f5ac0e3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2x\\sqrt{1+x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c01ef25-72cb-56e3-850f-f5b42b06cd2d" :answer/id #uuid "2c01ef25-72cb-56e3-850f-f5b42b06cd2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x(1+x)}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fffb130-9b68-531c-b156-aeb0418f3acf" :answer/id #uuid "5fffb130-9b68-531c-b156-aeb0418f3acf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{1+x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-578cf9cd-0a48-54e7-91c9-36e1da945aea" :answer/id #uuid "578cf9cd-0a48-54e7-91c9-36e1da945aea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2x\\sqrt{1+x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e95dd13d-e8b2-5d40-a5e7-9171f4068764" :answer/id #uuid "e95dd13d-e8b2-5d40-a5e7-9171f4068764" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{1+\\sqrt{x}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d8788c2a-c953-5587-a4b0-071fdea7bf08" :question/id #uuid "d8788c2a-c953-5587-a4b0-071fdea7bf08" :question/math-academy-id "q-313233" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(2x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{|x|}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(3\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|2x|\\sqrt{1+(2x)^{2}}})\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2|x|\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|x|}\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-64aa8422-e168-5f7f-b4b2-8eebac1df31f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-64aa8422-e168-5f7f-b4b2-8eebac1df31f" :answer-field/id #uuid "64aa8422-e168-5f7f-b4b2-8eebac1df31f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d3f5e67e-74f8-5482-8c10-428bbd5c2446" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d3f5e67e-74f8-5482-8c10-428bbd5c2446"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3f5e67e-74f8-5482-8c10-428bbd5c2446" :answer/id #uuid "d3f5e67e-74f8-5482-8c10-428bbd5c2446" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1+4x^2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-56abd260-e88d-5e15-85ad-d09d0617c5fa" :question/id #uuid "56abd260-e88d-5e15-85ad-d09d0617c5fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-341509" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=4\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{x}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[4\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{x})] \\\\  & =4\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[4]{x}\\sqrt{1-{(\\sqrt[4]{x})}^{2}}}]\\cdot {(\\sqrt[4]{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt[4]{x}\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt{x}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt[4]{{x}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt{x}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ddf9bdaf-0642-5a54-b951-2e09ed88b490"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ddf9bdaf-0642-5a54-b951-2e09ed88b490" :answer-field/id #uuid "ddf9bdaf-0642-5a54-b951-2e09ed88b490" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d9c27e1f-cdd4-55ba-829c-ded84bf3792a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d9c27e1f-cdd4-55ba-829c-ded84bf3792a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9c27e1f-cdd4-55ba-829c-ded84bf3792a" :answer/id #uuid "d9c27e1f-cdd4-55ba-829c-ded84bf3792a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt{x}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e713a272-c241-525b-b381-4fe5ba553286" :question/id #uuid "e713a272-c241-525b-b381-4fe5ba553286" :question/math-academy-id "q-341507" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{x}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{x})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}\\sqrt{1-{(\\sqrt[3]{x})}^{2}}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt[3]{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3x\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c873029d-a874-5147-92bb-16fa73e1b639"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c873029d-a874-5147-92bb-16fa73e1b639" :answer-field/id #uuid "c873029d-a874-5147-92bb-16fa73e1b639" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5928ab70-d114-5389-895b-065ef3d6aa09" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5928ab70-d114-5389-895b-065ef3d6aa09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5928ab70-d114-5389-895b-065ef3d6aa09" :answer/id #uuid "5928ab70-d114-5389-895b-065ef3d6aa09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3x\\sqrt{1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-83895ad6-7f6a-50d5-a3b6-af8475bcabcc" :question/id #uuid "83895ad6-7f6a-50d5-a3b6-af8475bcabcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-341514" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)] \\\\  & =2\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}}]\\cdot {(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡x}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-465397d6-a020-5d18-96a2-fa78f2cfd4d1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-465397d6-a020-5d18-96a2-fa78f2cfd4d1" :answer-field/id #uuid "465397d6-a020-5d18-96a2-fa78f2cfd4d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-240af742-1ebc-5760-a0f2-621341e0c161" :answer-field/choices ["answer-240af742-1ebc-5760-a0f2-621341e0c161"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-240af742-1ebc-5760-a0f2-621341e0c161" :answer/id #uuid "240af742-1ebc-5760-a0f2-621341e0c161" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sec x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-56f1a503-7979-5afa-a86c-36de0338e547" :question/id #uuid "56f1a503-7979-5afa-a86c-36de0338e547" :question/math-academy-id "q-95522" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡5x,$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡5x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡5x) \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{1}{(5x)\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}})\\cdot (5x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fd6a3276-afa5-552e-8370-0df3289262b0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fd6a3276-afa5-552e-8370-0df3289262b0" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd6a3276-afa5-552e-8370-0df3289262b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f756e2bb-9a31-56ee-859f-f341ea8ca2c9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7fdd1b05-efac-5cd2-b80d-adb096167f01" "answer-14e307ca-013b-55ec-82b5-1e7ce273b025" "answer-f3f36e7e-f5c6-5149-a6a3-fc6ab2a6b267" "answer-f756e2bb-9a31-56ee-859f-f341ea8ca2c9" "answer-9ba03e74-688b-57d5-9691-01500fb67606"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fdd1b05-efac-5cd2-b80d-adb096167f01" :answer/id #uuid "7fdd1b05-efac-5cd2-b80d-adb096167f01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14e307ca-013b-55ec-82b5-1e7ce273b025" :answer/id #uuid "14e307ca-013b-55ec-82b5-1e7ce273b025" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3f36e7e-f5c6-5149-a6a3-fc6ab2a6b267" :answer/id #uuid "f3f36e7e-f5c6-5149-a6a3-fc6ab2a6b267" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f756e2bb-9a31-56ee-859f-f341ea8ca2c9" :answer/id #uuid "f756e2bb-9a31-56ee-859f-f341ea8ca2c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ba03e74-688b-57d5-9691-01500fb67606" :answer/id #uuid "9ba03e74-688b-57d5-9691-01500fb67606" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186161288 :answer-field/choices 17592186161289] [:db/retract 17592186161288 :answer-field/choices 17592186161290] [:db/retract 17592186161288 :answer-field/choices 17592186161291] [:db/retract 17592186161288 :answer-field/choices 17592186161292] [:db/retract 17592186161288 :answer-field/choices 17592186161293] {:db/id 17592186162666 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A,$ $Σ,$ and $V$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ what is the second column of $U?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ and ${\\sigma }_{i}\\ne 0,$ then the $i$th column of $U$ can be found as\n\n$$\n{u}_{i}=\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{i}}A{v}_{i},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${v}_{i}$ is the $i$th column of the matrix $V.$\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=6$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=4.$ Therefore, the second column of $U$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161288 :answer-field/correct "answer-54deaa5d-b42c-582b-add4-d6575e45a079" :answer-field/choices ["answer-54deaa5d-b42c-582b-add4-d6575e45a079" "answer-5adca1a5-04fa-5979-ab07-c4374ef39ef9" "answer-8584a18f-938b-5b11-9a92-aea06357491c" "answer-875c7469-79dd-5306-8869-1ae4d067e4bf" "answer-e5b0b4f8-5d8c-5df5-bcb5-6a41d1765e47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54deaa5d-b42c-582b-add4-d6575e45a079" :answer/id #uuid "54deaa5d-b42c-582b-add4-d6575e45a079" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5adca1a5-04fa-5979-ab07-c4374ef39ef9" :answer/id #uuid "5adca1a5-04fa-5979-ab07-c4374ef39ef9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8584a18f-938b-5b11-9a92-aea06357491c" :answer/id #uuid "8584a18f-938b-5b11-9a92-aea06357491c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-875c7469-79dd-5306-8869-1ae4d067e4bf" :answer/id #uuid "875c7469-79dd-5306-8869-1ae4d067e4bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5b0b4f8-5d8c-5df5-bcb5-6a41d1765e47" :answer/id #uuid "e5b0b4f8-5d8c-5df5-bcb5-6a41d1765e47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162019 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-eeba80ad-bee9-5269-baef-fbd3bd2d6cda"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-eeba80ad-bee9-5269-baef-fbd3bd2d6cda" :question/id #uuid "eeba80ad-bee9-5269-baef-fbd3bd2d6cda" :question/math-academy-id "q-96323" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}73 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=9$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=1.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=81,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-81I & =[\\begin{aligned}73 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 9\\end{aligned}]-81[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -24 \\\\ -24 & -72\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-81I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-I & =[\\begin{aligned}73 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}72 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{27}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-92ef2ffd-6bce-5a3c-9878-3c95874f4572"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-92ef2ffd-6bce-5a3c-9878-3c95874f4572" :answer-field/id #uuid "92ef2ffd-6bce-5a3c-9878-3c95874f4572" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dafadf4d-f436-5d63-ba00-63f2baf56d03" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b2efb8c-2656-5a9e-bdf4-74177ad5bfa0" "answer-ada77caf-e98c-55fb-aefb-f3d728826900" "answer-e183294d-0160-5657-9a79-b2a38d4cd596" "answer-ab956e6c-1981-5cd4-973f-cb9d389db8f4" "answer-dafadf4d-f436-5d63-ba00-63f2baf56d03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b2efb8c-2656-5a9e-bdf4-74177ad5bfa0" :answer/id #uuid "2b2efb8c-2656-5a9e-bdf4-74177ad5bfa0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ada77caf-e98c-55fb-aefb-f3d728826900" :answer/id #uuid "ada77caf-e98c-55fb-aefb-f3d728826900" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e183294d-0160-5657-9a79-b2a38d4cd596" :answer/id #uuid "e183294d-0160-5657-9a79-b2a38d4cd596" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab956e6c-1981-5cd4-973f-cb9d389db8f4" :answer/id #uuid "ab956e6c-1981-5cd4-973f-cb9d389db8f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dafadf4d-f436-5d63-ba00-63f2baf56d03" :answer/id #uuid "dafadf4d-f436-5d63-ba00-63f2baf56d03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-7f97d789-9839-58fb-8e1d-4715f67e1d88" :activity/id #uuid "7f97d789-9839-58fb-8e1d-4715f67e1d88" :activity/title "Singular Value Decomposition of 2x2 Matrices" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050726 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-0fd9eb12-d390-5e28-b525-37da4fd463b3" "step-eee3bc90-1ac6-5bfc-8f49-7bbeddbe8022" "step-8a2108fe-05ce-5a0f-93ec-aefbea01ef7c" "step-ba507f27-de8d-57b9-abc6-5d9ed7fc3ec1" "step-9110dbbf-595e-5932-adab-f257d78e5fbe"] :activity/first-step "step-0fd9eb12-d390-5e28-b525-37da4fd463b3" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-0fd9eb12-d390-5e28-b525-37da4fd463b3" :step/id #uuid "0fd9eb12-d390-5e28-b525-37da4fd463b3" :step/content 17592186162666 :step/next "step-eee3bc90-1ac6-5bfc-8f49-7bbeddbe8022" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-eee3bc90-1ac6-5bfc-8f49-7bbeddbe8022" :step/id #uuid "eee3bc90-1ac6-5bfc-8f49-7bbeddbe8022" :step/content 17592186371290 :step/next "step-8a2108fe-05ce-5a0f-93ec-aefbea01ef7c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8a2108fe-05ce-5a0f-93ec-aefbea01ef7c" :step/id #uuid "8a2108fe-05ce-5a0f-93ec-aefbea01ef7c" :step/content "question-eeba80ad-bee9-5269-baef-fbd3bd2d6cda" :step/next "step-ba507f27-de8d-57b9-abc6-5d9ed7fc3ec1" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ba507f27-de8d-57b9-abc6-5d9ed7fc3ec1" :step/id #uuid "ba507f27-de8d-57b9-abc6-5d9ed7fc3ec1" :step/content 17592186371381 :step/next "step-9110dbbf-595e-5932-adab-f257d78e5fbe" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9110dbbf-595e-5932-adab-f257d78e5fbe" :step/id #uuid "9110dbbf-595e-5932-adab-f257d78e5fbe" :step/content 17592186496288 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186080087 :answer-field/choices 17592186080088] [:db/retract 17592186080087 :answer-field/choices 17592186080089] [:db/retract 17592186080087 :answer-field/choices 17592186080090] [:db/retract 17592186080087 :answer-field/choices 17592186080091] [:db/retract 17592186080087 :answer-field/choices 17592186080092] [:db/retract 17592186080999 :answer-field/choices 17592186081000] [:db/retract 17592186080999 :answer-field/choices 17592186081001] [:db/retract 17592186080999 :answer-field/choices 17592186081002] [:db/retract 17592186080999 :answer-field/choices 17592186081003] [:db/retract 17592186080999 :answer-field/choices 17592186081004] {:db/id 17592186083274 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e76e6bf7-d54d-5018-81b2-f60c46589b4a" "question-34ca4779-2bf7-5602-9812-9d6d9723327c" "question-f84ff77e-8bf5-5075-9613-766131045ace" "question-2a147b6b-b927-5c0b-b768-701655ad01fc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083067 :question/problem "Solve $x^3+x^2-9x-9=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-9x-9 & = \\\\ ({x}^{3}+{x}^{2})-(9x+9) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+1)-9(x+1) & = \\\\ (x+1)\\cdot {x}^{2}-(x+1)\\cdot 9 & = \\\\ (x+1)({x}^{2}-9) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(x+1)(x^2-9) = 0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x+1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =0 \\\\ x & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x^2-9)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-1, \\, \\pm  3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083246 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bb562da5-ef3b-592a-bfc0-4d26f88b1f50"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083042 :question/problem "Solve $2x^3+3x^2-8x-12=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed to factor the left side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-8x-12 & = \\\\ (2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2})-(8x+12) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}(2x+3)-4(2x+3) & = \\\\ (2x+3)\\cdot {x}^{2}-(2x+3)\\cdot 4 & = \\\\ (2x+3)({x}^{2}-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(2x+3)(x^2-4) = 0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(2x+3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x^2-4)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-2, \\; -\\dfrac{3}{2}, \\; 2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083275 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bbddec8f-0415-5a7f-a473-3ac96a89f653"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083068 :question/problem "Solve $-x^3-4x^2+5x+20=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$ to make the coefficient of the cubic term positive. This gives\n\n$$\nx^3+4x^2-5x-20=0.\n$$\n\nWe then proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x-20 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+4)-5(x+4) & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-5)(x+4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(x^2-5)(x+4)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x^2-5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =5 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x+4)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-4, \\pm \\sqrt 5.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083247 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-faa06da2-05be-56dd-9e44-883b8d4527f9" "question-f6abbc6d-e05c-5882-80a0-628ebefcab1b" "question-3e7651d9-4306-5281-ab2c-60e5fbcc4dde"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083043 :question/problem "Solve $8x^3+3=4x^2+6x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we subtract $4x^2$ and $6x$ from both sides to make the right side $0.$ To prepare for factoring by grouping, we make sure to write the resulting cubic in standard form.\n\n$$\n8x^3-4x^2-6x+3=0\n$$\n\nNext, we factor by grouping. Notice that when grouping the smaller terms, we factor out the negative sign.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-6x+3 & = \\\\ (8{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2})-(6x-3) & = \\\\ 4{x}^{2}(2x-1)-3(2x-1) & = \\\\ (2x-1)\\cdot 4{x}^{2}-(2x-1)\\cdot 3 & = \\\\ (2x-1)(4{x}^{2}-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set each factor equal to $0$ and solve.\n\n- Setting the factor $(2x-1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-1 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(4x^2-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-3 & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}, \\; \\dfrac12, \\; \\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-e76e6bf7-d54d-5018-81b2-f60c46589b4a" :question/id #uuid "e76e6bf7-d54d-5018-81b2-f60c46589b4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-72088" :question/problem "Solve $y$ if ${y}^{3}+5{y}^{2}-2y-10=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}+5{y}^{2}-2y-10 & = \\\\ ({y}^{3}+5{y}^{2})-(2y+10) & = \\\\ {y}^{2}(y+5)-2(y+5) & = \\\\ (y+5)\\cdot {y}^{2}-(y+5)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ (y+5)({y}^{2}-2) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(y+5)({y}^{2}-2)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(y+5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+5 & =0 \\\\ y & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({y}^{2}-2)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-2 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =2 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-5,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3e2b231c-9a04-5308-bd1d-78b7f972b284"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3e2b231c-9a04-5308-bd1d-78b7f972b284" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e2b231c-9a04-5308-bd1d-78b7f972b284" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-865b4b4c-4d95-5d8f-897e-8b44bf984a5e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d7a3fc0a-cc58-5e4b-89f5-8bf18d2b26fd" "answer-c204a35e-0f2e-5488-b2f7-6ab3e2814650" "answer-7f294bbf-c65c-5cdd-9fd2-b913e